cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use twosystems, please cite it as below."
title: "twosystems: a calibrated watchman for AI coding agents"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shashikant
    alias: shashikantdev3
repository-code: "https://github.com/shashikantdev3/twosystems"
url: "https://github.com/shashikantdev3/twosystems"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0-alpha.2
date-released: "2026-10-19"
abstract: >-
  twosystems watches AI coding agent sessions (Claude Code, GitHub Copilot,
  Codex), notices when the agent is stuck or when the work has moved on,
  suggests a better next step, and reports token savings, with a verified
  figure from a randomized holdout. Plain rules decide when to ask a small
  decision model (System 1); the user makes the final call. Calibrated
  thresholds and an optional larger model (System 2) are planned.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - claude-code
  - github-copilot
  - token-optimization
  - decision-models
  - calibration
  - llm-cost
